---
source: crates/shipper-cli/tests/e2e_expanded.rs
expression: normalize_stderr(&stdout)
---
Generate a shell completion script on stdout.

Supported shells: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh. The script is
printed, never installed — redirect it to wherever your shell loads
completions from.

EXAMPLES:
    # Bash, for the current user:
    shipper completion bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/shipper

    # Zsh, into a directory already on $fpath:
    shipper completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_shipper"


Usage: shipper-cli completion [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          Shell to generate completions for
          
          [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
      --config <CONFIG>
          Path to a custom configuration file (.shipper.toml)

      --manifest-path <MANIFEST_PATH>
          Path to the workspace Cargo.toml
          
          [default: Cargo.toml]

      --registry <REGISTRY>
          Cargo registry name (default: crates-io)

      --api-base <API_BASE>
          Registry API base URL (default: <https://crates.io>)

      --package <PACKAGES>
          Restrict to specific packages (repeatable). If omitted, publishes all publishable workspace members

      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>
          Directory for shipper state and receipts (default: .shipper)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: text (default) or json
          
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, json]

      --verbose
          Show detailed dependency analysis for plan command

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress informational output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
